From 737b84cdfd2fb49a0ee0bec124983100fe529f9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:14:44 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/24] kcm_colors: schemes read in slices after the first
 frame, accent color labelled, colour dialog built on use
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Gallery (docs/page-design.md section 5). Config keys (kdeglobals General/ColorScheme, AccentColor,
accentColorFromWallpaper, LastUsedCustomAccentColor), the scheme apply code, the accent-color service and the
kcolorschemeeditor are unchanged. NOT BUILT YET (owner stopped heavy work); checked statically only.

Moved / renamed:
- The accent color row (source combo + swatches) now starts with the label "Accent color:" (was an unlabelled combo box
  above the search field); its three choices keep their wording. Search and the All/Light/Dark filter stay in the header;
  Install from File… and Get New… stay page actions top right; Edit / Remove / Don't delete stay GridDelegate actions.
- Empty state: "No color schemes found" / "No color schemes match" (was an empty grid); busy indicator only after 150 ms.
- Relabel table: inventory/relabel/kcm_colors.tsv (outer repo). Inventory --strict: 29 rows ok, 0 lost
  (marker kept in editor/scmeditordialog.cpp for the unchanged Save As row).
- ia/duplicates.md lists no colors duplicate, so no link row was added. HIG ids: HIG-001, HIG-006; page-design sections 5, 7.

Speed (cause found in code, not measured):
- KCMColors::load() called ColorsModel::load() synchronously, before the page exists: for every *.colors file in every
  color-schemes data dir it opened a KConfig, built KColorScheme::createApplicationPalette (all colour sets and states),
  a second KColorScheme for the selection set, and a header-set check (colorsmodel.cpp load()), then sorted. About 30-50
  files on a normal install. Also Platform.ColorDialog was created with the page, inside the accent row.
- Now: ColorsModel::loadAsync() lists the files immediately and reads them in ~8 ms slices (loadNextBatch, same pattern
  as kcm_lookandfeel cf609d2); the finished list replaces the old one in one reset, sorted as before. New properties
  ColorsModel.loading / loaded; the grid has no model and currentIndex -1 until `loaded`. The scheme selection (and the
  "scheme is not installed" warning) is applied from the loadFinished signal (loadSelectedColorScheme). The synchronous
  ColorsModel::load() stays for install/edit, which need the list at once, and cancels a running background load.
  The colour dialog sits in a Loader that is active only while it is open.
- After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Not built yet; uncertain: Qt.labs.platform ColorDialog created from a Loader's sourceComponent and opened in
Component.onCompleted (same pattern as the FileDialog Loaders on these pages); that a second load() while the first
slices are pending restarts cleanly; FilterProxyModel's selectedSchemeIndex re-evaluation after the final reset on a
reload (unchanged from before).

